# Normalize all text files to LF in the repo AND on checkout, on every platform.
# This project deploys on Linux (Docker Alpine) and CI runs on Linux, so LF is
# the canonical line ending. Forcing eol=lf (rather than relying on each dev's
# core.autocrlf) keeps generated snapshots and the modules that produce them in
# lockstep — tests/telemetryContract.test.js compares public/llms.txt to the
# module's Markdown output byte-for-byte, which a CRLF checkout would break.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending-normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
